  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday night through next Wednesday)\nIssued at 1157 PM CDT Tue Jul 28 2026\n\nThe \"dog days of summer\" pattern of hot and dry conditions will \ncontinue through at least Friday due to a persistent upper-level \nridge over the Desert Southwest and west Texas.  This ridge has \n500mb heights of 594dam while 850mb temperatures of 23 to 26 deg C \nshould remain over west Texas. Southerly winds and mostly sunny \nskies, should continue to result in high temperatures in the upper \n90s to low 100s. The highest mid-level heights will be located over \nnorthwest Texas and the Big Country and this is where the warmest \nconditions should occur. There is a medium (50-75%) chance of \ntemperatures reaching 105 degrees or higher on Thursday and Friday, \nwhich would meet heat advisory criteria.\n\nThe upper-level pattern looks to shift slightly for this weekend. \nModels are in overall agreement of a strong trough dropping down \nfrom the Upper Midwest to the Ohio Valley Saturday into Sunday. This \nfeature should force the ridge westward and push a weak surface cold \nfront southward into central Texas by Saturday night. Some low \nchances (<15%) exist for light rain showers along this front for \nSaturday into Saturday night, but nothing heavy is expected due to \nthe lack of upper-level support. While upper-level heights should \nlower a bit, temperatures should only be a few degrees cooler for \nSunday and Monday.",
